{"slug":"rotate-array-right","title":"Rotate Array to the Right","topic":"arrays-strings","difficulty":"easy","order":103,"tags":["arrays","rotation","modulo"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Rotation is index arithmetic","body":["Rotating an array to the right by `k` moves every element `k` places forward, and the elements that fall off the end come back at the start. The element that ends at position `i` is the one that started at position `(i - k) mod n`.","Rotating by `n` gives the same array again, so first replace `k` by `k % n`. That also makes a huge `k` harmless.",{"code":"k %= n\nrotated = a[n - k:] + a[:n - k]"}]},"statement":["Rotate an array of `n` integers to the right by `k` places and print the result."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n` and `k`.","The second line has `n` integers."],"outputFormat":["Print the rotated array on one line."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 1000","0 <= k <= 10^9","-10^9 <= each number <= 10^9"],"examples":[{"input":"5 2\n1 2 3 4 5\n","output":"4 5 1 2 3\n","note":"The last two elements, 4 and 5, move to the front."}],"hints":["After one rotation to the right, the last element becomes the first.","Rotating by n changes nothing, so use `k % n`.","The element at output position i is `a[(i - k + n) % n]`."],"starter":{"python":"n, k = map(int, input().split())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    long long k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long k = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["Reduce `k` modulo `n`. The new array is the last `k` elements followed by the first `n - k` elements."],"complexity":"Time O(n), space O(n).","code":{"python":"n, k = map(int, input().split())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nk %= n\nprint(*(a[n - k:] + a[:n - k]))\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    long long k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    k %= n;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        cout << a[(i - k + n) % n] << (i + 1 < n ? \" \" : \"\\n\");\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long k = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        k %= n;\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            sb.append(a[(int) ((i - k + n) % n)]).append(i + 1 < n ? \" \" : \"\\n\");\n        }\n        System.out.print(sb);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"5 2\n1 2 3 4 5\n","output":"4 5 1 2 3\n"},{"input":"1 7\n9\n","output":"9\n"},{"input":"4 0\n1 2 3 4\n","output":"1 2 3 4\n"},{"input":"4 4\n1 2 3 4\n","output":"1 2 3 4\n"},{"input":"4 1000000000\n1 2 3 4\n","output":"1 2 3 4\n"},{"input":"5 38\n-7 7 -3 -6 0\n","output":"-3 -6 0 -7 7\n"},{"input":"2 30\n-7 -9\n","output":"-7 -9\n"},{"input":"2 9\n0 -2\n","output":"-2 0\n"},{"input":"2 16\n3 5\n","output":"3 5\n"},{"input":"8 35\n2 0 2 -1 -6 -7 8 -9\n","output":"-7 8 -9 2 0 2 -1 -6\n"},{"input":"1000 999\n668908581 -49193040 -24945521 -695683175 510806483 161877090 -841159500 -464486425 -869191593 685921848 337620930 810570517 300076070 -497128853 -650120537 -307430455 -530031470 -631911133